{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795497511066,"sessionID":"ses_df4027bf4fferxSUxHfY0Zqzpi","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9cd236d137209ca4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /travail && .venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport pymupdf, glob, os\nfor ds in ['dos-007']:\n    for p in sorted(glob.glob(f'fourni/{ds}/*.pdf')):\n        d=pymupdf.open(p)\n        print('#'*30, p, len(d), 'pages')\n        for i,pg in enumerate(d):\n            t=pg.get_text()\n            print(f'--- page {i+1}: textlen={len(t)} images={len(pg.get_images())}')\n            print(t[:1500])\nEOF"},"output":"############################## fourni/dos-007/piece-01.pdf 5 pages\n--- page 1: textlen=731 images=4\nSERVICE REPORT\nMaintenance and metrological check\nREPORT REFERENCE\nPF-RI-2025-4742\nPO NUMBER\nPO-964865\nPAGE\n1/5\nMANUFACTURER\nNerulquin\nASSET NO.\nINV-88173\nEQUIPMENT\n—\nUNIT ID\nNE214179\nJOB NO.\nAFF-48402\nDATE OF INTERVENTION\n—\nREQUEST DATE\n22 Sep 2025\nISSUE DATE\n30 Sep 2025\nLOCATION\nHexham Site\nCUSTOMER\nMabrix Beverages\nHead office: Livingston\nINSTALLATION\nLine 3\ndiaphragm metering pump\nSCOPE\nMetrological check and preventive\nmaintenance of dosing equipment\nSTATUS\nCompliant\nNon-compliant\nTo be reviewed\nSign-off\nPrepared by\nChecked by\nApproved by\nName\nAoife Redding\nGrace Doyle\nCallum Brennan\nDate\n30 Sep 2025\n30 Sep 2025\n6 Oct 2025\nSignature\nRev.\nDate\nDescription\nA\n30 Sep 2025\nFirst issue\nB\n30 Sep 2025\nCorrected after review\n\n--- page 2: textlen=1339 images=1\nPrapax Field Services\nDocument ref. PF-RI-2025-4742  Revision B\nPrinted on 8 Oct 2025\nPage 2/5\n1. Visit\nFIELD TEAM\nAoife Redding (lead)\nLiam Kerrigan (assistant)\nREQUESTED BY\nRyan Calloway\nTIMES\nArrival: 8 h 00\nDuration: 3 h\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nprobe thermometer\nJuvanvex\nIN-93924\n7 Jun 2025\nreference pressure\ngauge\nPolonis\nEQ-54190\n8 Aug 2025\nBackground and equipment\nNo abnormal noise or heating was observed during dry runs. The visit concerns the diaphragm metering pump Calultik 600. It is driven\nby a Kaldor motor, type M85-4P. The night shift was informed of the adjustments made. No leak was found on the fittings after\nrepressurisation.\nCourse of the visit\nGuards were refitted and their interlocks checked before restart. The visit took place on 26 September 2025, following a request of 22\nSeptember 2025. The customer's head office is in Livingston. Frame fixings and hoses were visually inspected; no corrosion was found.\nSensor wiring was inspected and connectors tightened.\nAdjustments and results\nThe production manager was kept informed at each step of the visit. On arrival the delivered quantity averaged 20.8 mL. The customer's\ntarget value is 20 cm³. The deviation allowed by the customer's specification is ± 2.5 %. Cycle counter readings were entered in the\nmachine logbook.\n\n--- page 3: textlen=1108 images=0\nPrapax Field Services\nDocument ref. PF-RI-2025-4742  Revision B\nPrinted on 8 Oct 2025\nPage 3/5\n2. Measurements\nTable 1 - Readings\nParameter\nAs found\nAs left\nMean\nas left\nTolerance\nE1\nE2\nE3\nE1\nE2\nE3\nDose volume\n20.6 mL\n21.1 mL\n20.7 mL\n20.6 mL\n20.5 mL\n19.8 mL\n20.3 mL\nFlow rate\n436 mL/min\nn.m.\n—\n—\nOperating pressure\n4.4 bar\n—\n—\n—\nTemperature\n28.7 °C\n30.2 °C\n—\n—\nTable 2 - Ratings\nRating\nValue\nModel range (OEM)\n1 – 20 mL\nTank capacity\n60 L\nLine volume\n290 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 0.2 mL\nMax. flow\n970 mL/min\nMax. allowable pressure\n12.5 bar\nRelief valve setting\n7.6 bar\nReplacements\nThe manufacturer's documentation was available on site and up to date. Part NE-986-R (head gasket) was inspected and found in good\ncondition.\nField team\nMachine noise level in operation remained as usual. A manual-mode test run preceded the return to automatic operation. Liam Kerrigan\ntook part in the visit, at the request of Ryan Calloway. The technician checked that no air bubbles were present in the circuit before each\nseries of measurements. Production data from recent weeks was reviewed with the customer.\n\n--- page 4: textlen=381 images=1\nPrapax Field Services\nDocument ref. PF-RI-2025-4742  Revision B\nPrinted on 8 Oct 2025\nPage 4/5\n3. Layout diagram\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6 outlet nozzle.\nTechnician's opinion\nSuction filters were removed, rinsed and refitted. Tests were run until readings were stable. The circuit was purged until a steady flow\nwas obtained.\n\n--- page 5: textlen=951 images=2\nPrapax Field Services\nDocument ref. PF-RI-2025-4742  Revision B\nPrinted on 8 Oct 2025\nPage 5/5\n4. Parts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nNE-986-R\nhead gasket\ninspected, kept\n470.12 €\nNE-124-R\ndiaphragm\nordered (not fitted)\n419.26 €\nNE-854-K\nsuction valve\nquoted\n335.34 €\n5. Observations\nAdditional information, operating pressure as left: 5.7 bar.\nAdditional information, item code of the replaced part: NE-813-C.\nThe upstream conveyor Ulvagen C74 (flow 646 mL/min, pressure 7.8 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop air network\nruns at 7.0 bar.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: 26 Sep 2026.\nApproval workflow\nAccess to the machine was granted after electrical and pneumatic lock-out by the line manager. Guide lubrication was topped up as per\nthe manual. The report was reviewed on 30 September 2025.\n6. Signatures\nResponsible technician : Aoife Redding\nCustomer approval: Callum Brennan\n\n############################## fourni/dos-007/piece-02.pdf 4 pages\n--- page 1: textlen=1851 images=1\nPRAANET METROLOGY\nPrinted on 2024-12-13\nsheet 1/4\nReport PM-RI-2024-8565\nTECHNICAL INTERVENTION REPORT\nReport reference : PM-RI-2024-8565\nPO number : PO-506512\nJob no. : AFF-46602\nCustomer : Mabrix Beverages, Head office: Hexham\nSite : Hexham Site\nInstallation : Line 3, diaphragm meterin