 :\n09/03/2025\nIssue date :\n19/03/2025\nDate of intervention :\n—\nReadings summary (provisional)\nDose volume\n20.1 mL\nBackground and equipment\nThe previous preventive visit only involved cleaning the fluid circuit. The visit concerns the dosing equipment of line 3. It is\ndriven by a Juvanvex motor, type L85-4P. The technician checked that no air bubbles were present in the circuit before\neach series of measurements.\nCourse of the visit\nThe electrical cabinet ventilation was dusted and its filter checked. The visit to the customer, Hexham Site, took place on\n14 March 2025, following a request of 9 March 2025. The customer's head office is in Livingston. The prevention plan was\nreviewed with the site safety department before work started.\nReadings\nParameter\nValue\nDose volume, as found, E1-E3\n21.6  21.7  21.2\nDose volume, as left, E1-E3\n20.1  20.3  20.8\nDose volume, mean as left (mL)\n20.4\nFlow rate (L/min), as found\n0.392\nFlow rate (L/min), as left\n0.448\nOperating pressure (bar), as found\n4.8\nOperating pressure (bar), as left\n5.4\nProduct temperature (°C)\n20.9\nMeasurement table values prevail; the summary shows provisional readings.\nRating\nValue\nNomin\n--- page 2: textlen=1273 images=2\nDORORQUIN FIELD SERVICES  |  SERVICE REPORT\nPrinted on 31/03/2025\n2 / 3\nDiagram\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6 outlet nozzle.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nreference pressure\ngauge\nJuvanvex\nEQ-57336\n03/06/2024\nprobe thermometer\nNerra\nIN-19503\n10/01/2025\nParts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nNE-796-R\ndiaphragm\nreplaced\n30.46 €\nNE-983-K\ndischarge valve\ninspected, kept\n504.74 €\nNE-653-A\nsuction valve\nordered (not fitted)\n386.98 €\nNE-402-C\nhead gasket\nquoted\n361.10 €\nField team\nGuards were refitted and their interlocks checked before restart. Hannah Ainsley took part in the visit, at the request of\nDeclan Calloway.\nTechnician's opinion\nAdjustments were made with the machine stopped, then checked in production. Tests were run until readings were stable.\nApproval workflow\nThe night shift was informed of the adjustments made. The report was reviewed on 20 March 2025.\nNotes\nNote, report reference: DF-RI-2025-3976.\nNote, serial number: NE214179.\nFor the record, status: Compliant.\nThe upstream conveyor Kesinlor C77 (flow 0.883 L/min, pressure 6.9 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the workshop\nair network runs at 7.0 bar.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\n\n--- page 3: textlen=169 images=2\nDORORQUIN FIELD SERVICES  |  SERVICE REPORT\nPrinted on 31/03/2025\n3 / 3\nNext preventive visit: 12/09/2025.\nLead technician : Megan Mahon\nCustomer approval: Chloe Stroud\n\n############################## fourni/dos-007/piece-04.pdf 4 pages\n--- page 1: textlen=1855 images=1\nPRAANET METROLOGY\nPrinted on 2024-12-17\nsheet 1/4\nReport PM-RI-2024-8576\nTECHNICAL INTERVENTION REPORT\nDocument no. : PM-RI-2024-8576\nSupersedes : PM-RI-2024-8565\nPO number : PO-199868\nJob no. : AFF-87554\nCustomer : Mabrix Beverages, Head office: Dundee\nLocation : Hexham Site\nInstallation : Line 4, diaphragm metering pump\nUnit : Calultik 600\nUnit ID : NE214179\nAsset no. : INV-58221\nRequest date : 2024-11-18\nIssue date : 2024-11-29\nService date : 2024-11-25\nThe prevention plan was reviewed with the site safety department before work\nstarted. Sensor wiring was inspected and connectors tightened. The production\nmanager was kept informed at each step of the visit.\nI. BACKGROUND\nBackground and equipment\nThe night shift was informed of the adjustments made. The visit concerns the\ndosing equipment of line 4, built by Nerulquin. It is driven by a Corlix motor,\ntype M110-4P. No leak was found on the fittings after repressurisation. The\nequipment runs on two shifts, five days a week, for liquid product packaging.\nMachine noise level in operation remained as usual. The customer was briefed on\nthe points of attention noted during the visit.\nCourse of the visit\nChecks were carried out with calibrated instruments; certificates are\navailable to the customer. The electrical cabinet ventilation was dusted and\nits filter checked. The service request was received on 18 November 2024. The\ncustomer's head office is in Dundee.\nNo abnormal noise or heating was observed during dry runs. PLC settings\n--- page 2: textlen=1648 images=1\nPRAANET METROLOGY\nPrinted on 2024-12-17\nsheet 2/4\nReport PM-RI-2024-8576\nQuantity\nValue\nUnit\nObservation\nFill volume as left, trial 1\n—\nFill volume as left, trial 2\n—\nFill volume as left, trial 3\n—\nFill volume mean as left\n—\nsee diagram\nFlow rate as left\nn.m.\nProduct temperature\n24.7\nLine volume\n236\nTank capacity\n200\nFlow rate as found\n424 mL/min\nOperating pressure as left\n—\nOperating pressure as found\n4.4 bar\nIII. WORK PERFORMED\nAdjustments and results\nThe work station was left clean and clear at the end of the visit. On arrival\nthe delivered quantity averaged 18.5 mL. Pressure settled at 5.4 bar, the\nrelief valve remaining set at 9.6 bar. Access to the machine was granted after\nelectrical and pneumatic lock-out by the line manager. The manufacturer's\ndocumentation was available on site and up to date. Frame fixings and hoses\nwere visually inspected; no corrosion was found.\nReplacements\nProducts dosed on this line are aqueous and of low viscosity; no hazardous\nproduct was in the circuit during the visit. Part NE-663-A (diaphragm) was\ninspected and found in good condition. Operators reported short stoppages at\nshift start, with no alarm message. Production data from recent weeks was\nreviewed with the customer.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nreference\npressure gauge\nMabzor\nET-97244\n2024-01-30\nprecision\nbalance\nMabbel\nIN-80642\n2024-06-23\nRating\nValue\nNominal volume\n20 cm³\nMPE\n± 0.5 mL\nModel range (OEM)\n1 – 20 mL\nTank capacity\n200 L\nLine volume\n236 m\n--- page 3: textlen=1451 images=1\nPRAANET METROLOGY\nPrinted on 2024-12-17\nsheet 3/4\nReport PM-RI-2024-8576\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6 outlet\nnozzle.\nV. OBSERVATIONS\nFor the record, outcome: Non-compliant.\nThe upstream conveyor Dravex C12 (flow 1,129 mL/min, pressure 6.8 bar) is\noutside the scope of this visit; the workshop air network runs at 7.0 bar.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: 2025-11-25.\nField team\nThe technician checked that no air bubbles were present in the circuit before\neach series of measurements. Liam Doyle took part in the visit, at the request\nof Rhys Pryce. Machine safety labels are legible and complete. A manual-mode\ntest run preceded the return to automatic operation. Dried product residue on\nthe frame was cleaned off.\nTechnician's opinion\nGuide lubrication was topped up as per the manual. Adjustments were made with\nthe machine stopped, then checked in production. Cleaning-in-place\ninstructions were reminded to the production team. Quick couplings were\ndismantled, cleaned and refitted with a compatible lubricant. Tests were run\nuntil readings were stable.\nApproval workflow\nGuards were refitted and their interlocks checked before restart. The report\nwas reviewed on 30 November 2024. The work area was cordoned off for the whole\nduration of the visit. The circuit was purged until a steady flow was obtained.\nParts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\n\n--- page 4: textlen=342 images=2\nPRAANET METROLOGY\nPrinted on 2024-12-17\nsheet 4/4\nReport PM-RI-2024-8576\nNE-225-B\ndischarge valve\nreplaced\n605.55 €\nNE-663-A\ndiaphragm\ninspected, kept\n140.11 €\nNE-161-B\nsuction valve\nordered (not fitted)\n163.86 €\nNE-829-C\nhead gasket\nquoted\n635.75 €\nVI. CONCLUSION\nTechnician:\nCustomer approval: Ethan Thornley\nValidation date : ____________\n\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /travail &&