\nTank capacity\n80 L\nLine volume\n561 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 0.2 mL\nMax. flow\n7680 mL/min\nMax. allowable pressure\n7.0 bar\nRelief valve setting\n4.0 bar\nAdjustments and results\nPLC settings were not changed during the visit. After several stroke adjustments, the delivered\nquantity settled at 24.6 mL on average, against 25.8 mL on arrival. Pressure settled at 2.5 bar,\nthe relief valve remaining set at 4.0 bar.\nReplacements\nNo leak was found on the fittings after repressurisation. Part CO-914-K (piston seal) was\ninspected and found in good condition.\nDiagram\n\n===== PAGE 2 (textlen=1408, images=2) =====\nTORIOBEL SERVICES LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. TS-RI-2025-7849\nPrinted on 19/05/2025\n2 / 3\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6 outlet nozzle.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nreference\npressure gauge\nPolamos\nIN-44623\n08/01/2025\nprobe thermometer\nCalultik\nEQ-59255\n07/09/2024\nParts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nCO-217-A\ndosing nozzle\nreplaced\n637.21 €\nCO-914-K\npiston seal\ninspected, kept\n466.18 €\nCO-943-D\nreturn spring\nordered (not fitted)\n439.17 €\nCO-173-E\ncheck valve\nquoted\n206.37 €\nField team\nGuide lubrication was topped up as per the manual. James Calloway led the visit with the support\nof Olivia Kerrigan, at the request of Daniel Ashby. Demineralised water at room temperature was\nused for all tests.\nTechnician's opinion\nThe night shift was informed of the adjustments made. Tests were run until readings were stable.\nApproval workflow\nGuards were refitted and their interlocks checked before restart. The report was reviewed on 17\nMay 2025. Sensor wiring was inspected and connectors tightened.\nNotes\nAdditional information, status: Compliant.\nFor the record, manufacturer: Corlix.\nThe upstream conveyor Vernis C23 (flow 9380 mL/min, pressure 4.4 bar) is outside the scope of\nthis visit; the workshop air network runs at 6.0 bar.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: 16/05/2026.\n\n===== PAGE 3 (textlen=162, images=2) =====\nTORIOBEL SERVICES LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. TS-RI-2025-7849\nPrinted on 19/05/2025\n3 / 3\nTechnician:\nCustomer approval: Chloe Keane\nValidation date : 18/05/2025\n\n===== PAGE 1 (textlen=1670, images=1) =====\nMirlor Metrology\nReport no. MM-RI-2025-8108\nPrinted on 29/05/2025\nPage 1/3\nSERVICE REPORT\nMaintenance and metrological check of dosing equipment\nReport reference\nMM-RI-2025-8108\nSupersedes\nMM-RI-2025-7975\nPO number\nPO-653367\nJob no.\nAFF-68089\nCustomer\nZenbel Beverages ; Head office: Wexford\nInstallation\nLine 2 ; piston filler\nUnit\nLornet 600\nMake\nCorlix\nSerial number\nn/a\nAsset no.\nINV-59188\nMPE\n± 0.625 mL\nRequest date\n08/05/2025\nIssue date\n19/05/2025\nDate of intervention\nn/a\nBackground and equipment\nThe circuit was purged until a steady flow was obtained. The manufacturer's documentation was available on site\nand up to date. The visit concerns the dosing equipment of line 2, whose plate reads CO463282. It is driven by a\nPramar motor, type M95-2P. Quick couplings were dismantled, cleaned and refitted with a compatible lubricant.\n1. Measurements\nParameter\nAs found\nAs-left trials\nMean as left\nMPE\nDose volume (mL)\n23\n24.5 / 24.4 / 25.2\n24.7\nDelivery rate (mL/min)\n2,800\n3,310\nOperating pressure (bar)\n2.3\n3.0\nRatings\nRating\nValue\nModel range (OEM)\n5 – 500 mL\nTank capacity\n80 L\nLine volume\n266 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 0.2 mL\nMax. flow\n5,720 mL/min\nMax. allowable pressure\n7.0 bar\nRelief valve setting\n4.4 bar\nCourse of the visit\nCleaning-in-place instructions were reminded to the production team. Adjustments were made with the machine\nstopped, then checked in production. The visit to the customer, Shannon Works, took place on 16 May 2025,\nfollowing a request of 8 May 2025. The customer's head office is in Wexford. Guards were refitted and their\ninterlocks checked before restart. Demineralised water at room temperature was used for all tests.\n\n===== PAGE 2 (textlen=1417, images=2) =====\nMirlor Metrology\nReport no. MM-RI-2025-8108\nPrinted on 29/05/2025\nPage 2/3\nAdjustments and results\nA manual-mode test run preceded the return to automatic operation. Emergency stops were tested and work\ncorrectly. On arrival the delivered quantity averaged 23 mL. Machine safety labels are legible and complete.\n2. Layout diagram\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6 outlet nozzle.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nreference pressure\ngauge\nNerra\nET-63921\n13/12/2024\nprobe thermometer\nJuvanvex\nET-85678\n15/03/2025\n3. Report\nReplacements\nThe technician checked that no air bubbles were present in the circuit before each series of measurements.\nProduction data from recent weeks was reviewed with the customer. Part CO-499-R (return spring) was inspected\nand found in good condition. No abnormal noise or heating was observed during dry runs.\nField team\nProducts dosed on this line are aqueous and of low viscosity; no hazardous product was in the circuit during the\nvisit. The production manager was kept informed at each step of the visit. Daniel Kerrigan took part in the visit, at\nthe request of Ethan Stroud.\nTechnician's opinion\nCycle counter readings were entered in the machine logbook. Dried product residue on the frame was cleaned off.\nAt the end of the tests, the equipment may return to production subject to an early follow-up visit.\n\n===== PAGE 3 (textlen=821, images=2) =====\nMirlor Metrology\nReport no. MM-RI-2025-8108\nPrinted on 29/05/2025\nPage 3/3\nApproval workflow\nThe previous preventive visit only involved cleaning the fluid circuit. The report was reviewed on 21 May 2025.\n4. Parts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nCO-418-C\ncheck valve\nreplaced\n295.23 €\nCO-499-R\nreturn spring\ninspected, kept\n430.99 €\nCO-549-B\npiston seal\nordered (not fitted)\n173.52 €\nCO-651-D\ndosing nozzle\nquoted\n479.29 €\n5. Observations\nAdditional information, validation date: 27 May 2025.\nThe upstream conveyor Nerra C45 (flow 7,070 mL/min, pressure 5.7 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the\nworkshop air network runs at 7.0 bar.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: 16/05/2026.\n6. Conclusion\nResponsible technician : Declan Ainsley\nCustomer approval: Olivia Brennan\n\n===== PAGE 1 (textlen=1940, images=1) =====\nTORIOBEL SERVICES LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. TS-RI-2024-8901\nPrinted on 19/11/2024\n1 / 3\nSERVICE REPORT\nInspection and maintenance\nReport reference :\nTS-RI-2024-8901\nPO number :\nPO-296625\nJob no. :\nAFF-91341\nCustomer :\nZenbel Beverages, Head office:\nWrexham\nInstallation :\nLine 2, piston filler\nEquipment :\nLornet 600\nManufacturer :\nCorlix\nSerial number :\n—\nAsset no. :\nINV-45379\nRequest date :\n01/11/2024\nIssue date :\n11/11/2024\nBackground and equipment\nThe production manager was kept informed at each step of the visit. The visit concerns the\ndosing equipment of line 2. It is driven by a Calultik motor, type T104-2P.\nCourse of the visit\nMachine safety labels are legible and complete. The visit to the customer, Shannon Works, took\nplace on 9 November 2024, following a request of 1 November 2024. The customer's head office is\nin Wrexham.\nReadings\nParameter\nValue\nDose volume, as found, E1-E3\n24  24.1  24.5 mL\nDose volume, as left, E1-E3\n25.3  25.4  24.9 mL\nDose volume, mean as left\n25.2 mL\nFlow rate, as found\n165 L/h\nFlow rate, as left\n—\nOperating pressure, as found\n2.6 bar\nOperating pressure, as left\n3.0 bar\nProduct temperature (°C)\n22.6\nRating\nValue\nNominal volume\n25 mL\nTolerance\n± 0.625 cm³\nModel range (OEM)\n5 – 500 mL\nTank capacity\n20 L\nLine volume\n689 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 0.1 mL\nMax. flow\n364.2 L/h\nMax. allowable pressure\n8.0 bar\nRelief valve setting\n5.4 bar\nAdjustments and results\nProducts dosed on this line are aqueous and of low viscosity; no hazardous product was in the\ncircuit during the visit. On arrival the delivered quantity averaged 24.2 mL. The equipment then\ndelivers 184.8 L/h, well below its maximum of 364.2 L/h.\nReplacements\nQuick couplings were dismantled, cleaned and refitted with a compatible lubricant. No\nreplacement was needed; part CO-378-E (return spring) was nevertheless ordered as a precaution.\nPart CO-485-R (check valve) was inspected and found in good condition.\nDiagram\n\n===== PAGE 2 (textlen=1115, images=3) =====\nTORIOBEL SERVICES LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. TS-RI-2024-8901\nPrinted on 19/11/2024\n2 / 3\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6 outlet nozzle.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nEquipment rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nreference\npressure gauge\nPolamos\nIN-61723\n09/09/2024\nprecision balance\nPraiorix\nET-54243\n20/09/2024\nParts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nCO-485-R\ncheck valve\ninspected, kept\n381.26 €\nCO-378-E\nreturn spring\nordered (not fitted)\n324.61 €\nCO-766-K\ndosing nozzle\nquoted\n317.76 €\nNo part was replaced during this visit.\nField team\nThe electrical cabinet ventilation was dusted and its filter checked. Erin Pryce took part in\nthe visit, at the request of Olivia Stroud.\nTechnician's opinion\nNo abnormal noise or heating was observed during dry runs. At the end of the tests, the\nequipment may return to production without restriction. The previous preventive visit only\ninvolved cleaning the fluid circuit.\nApproval workflow\nA manual-mode test run preceded the return to automatic operation. The report was reviewed on 14\nNovember 2024.\nNotes\n\n===== PAGE 3 (textlen=452, images=2) =====\nTORIOBEL SERVICES LTD  |  SERVICE REPORT\nRef. TS-RI-2024-8901\nPrinted on 19/11/2024\n3 / 3\nThe upstream conveyor Belira C38 (flow 318.6 L/h, pressure 5.3 bar