{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795497528760,"sessionID":"ses_df4027bf4fferxSUxHfY0Zqzpi","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-97b2b4c2dfd4a4fb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /travail && for f in work/txt/dos-015__*.txt work/txt/dos-017__piece-02.txt work/txt/dos-017__piece-03.txt work/txt/dos-017__piece-05.txt; do echo \"################ $f\"; cat \"$f\"; done"},"output":"################ work/txt/dos-015__piece-01.txt\n\n===== PAGE 1 (textlen=1736, images=1) =====\nMirlor Metrology\nReport no. MM-RI-2024-4965\nPrinted on 28/11/2024\nPage 1/3\nSERVICE REPORT\nMaintenance and metrological check of dosing equipment\nDocument no.\nMM-RI-2024-4965\nPO number\nPO-876673\nJob no.\nAFF-73166\nCustomer\nBelquin Foods ; Head office: Carlow\nSite\nWexford Works\nInstallation\nLine 2 ; rotary filling machine\nManufacturer\nn/a\nAsset no.\nINV-66854\nRequest date\n18/11/2024\nIssue date\n22/11/2024\nBackground and equipment\nGuards were refitted and their interlocks checked before restart. Quick couplings were dismantled, cleaned and\nrefitted with a compatible lubricant. The visit concerns the dosing equipment of line 2, built by Tortis. It is driven by\na Polonis motor, type K68-2P. The night shift was informed of the adjustments made.\n1. Measurements\nParameter\nAs found\nAs-left trials\nMean as left\nTolerance\nDose volume (mL) - head 1\n776.9\n745 / 744.2 / 745.2\n744.8\nDose volume (mL) - head 2\n776.9\n743.3 / 743.2 / 743.7\n743.4\nDose volume (mL) - head 3\n776.9\n740.8 / 744.1 / 743.8\n742.9\nDose volume (mL) - head 4\n776.9\n751 / 749.4 / 749.9\n750.1\nOverall mean\n745.3\nThroughput (mL/min)\n13,250\nn/a\nOperating pressure (bar)\n0.5\n0.6\nRatings\nRating\nValue\nTarget volume\n750 mL\nModel range (OEM)\n100 – 1,000 mL\nTank capacity\n1,000 L\nLine volume\n3,420 mL\nExpanded uncertainty (k = 2)\n± 4.1 mL\nMax. flow\n34,550 mL/min\nMax. allowable pressure\n2.0 bar\nRelief valve setting\n0.8 bar\nCourse of the visit\nAccess to the machine was granted after electrical and pneumatic lock-out by the line manager. Adjustments were\nmade with the machine stopped, then checked in production. The service request was received on 18 November\n2024. The customer's head office is in Carlow. The manufacturer's documentation was available on site and up to\ndate.\n\n===== PAGE 2 (textlen=1171, images=2) =====\nMirlor Metrology\nReport no. MM-RI-2024-4965\nPrinted on 28/11/2024\nPage 2/3\nAdjustments and results\nGuide lubrication was topped up as per the manual. On arrival the delivered quantity averaged 776.9 mL. The\ndeviation allowed by the customer's specification is ± 2 %. A manual-mode test run preceded the return to\nautomatic operation.\n2. Layout diagram\nKey: 1 tank; 2 supply line; 3 dosing unit; 4 pressure gauge; 5 flow direction; 6 outlet nozzle.\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nprobe thermometer\nLoremar\nEQ-29553\n09/06/2024\nreference pressure\ngauge\nKaldor\nET-96461\n06/08/2024\n3. Report\nReplacements\nNo leak was found on the fittings after repressurisation. Part TO-456-K (level probe) was inspected and found in\ngood condition.\nField team\nDried product residue on the frame was cleaned off. Emergency stops were tested and work correctly. Callum\nHollis took part in the visit, at the request of Declan Ainsley.\nTechnician's opinion\nNo abnormal noise or heating was observed during dry runs. The technician checked that no air bubbles were\npresent in the circuit before each series of measurements. Tests were run until readings were stable.\n\n===== PAGE 3 (textlen=1027, images=2) =====\nMirlor Metrology\nReport no. MM-RI-2024-4965\nPrinted on 28/11/2024\nPage 3/3\nApproval workflow\nSensor wiring was inspected and connectors tightened. The report was reviewed on 25 November 2024. Cycle\ncounter readings were entered in the machine logbook.\n4. Parts\nPart no.\nDescription\nAction\nUnit price\nTO-456-K\nlevel probe\ninspected, kept\n181.54 €\nTO-647-B\nhead solenoid valve\nordered (not fitted)\n325.86 €\nTO-599-K\nfilling cannula\nquoted\n627.72 €\n5. Observations\nFor the record, serial number: TO312707.\nNote, equipment: Helorquin 160.\nNote, part reference of the replaced part: TO-934-A.\nNote, throughput as left: 14,150 mL/min.\nAdditional information, service date: 20 November 2024.\nThe upstream conveyor Lumonet C39 (flow 32,950 mL/min, pressure 2.7 bar) is outside the scope of this visit; the\nworkshop air network runs at 6.0 bar.\nOn arrival the equipment was rated non-compliant.\nNext preventive visit: 21/05/2025.\n6. Conclusion\nResult\nCompliant\nTechnician:\nCustomer approval: Liam Whitfield\nValidation date : 26/11/2024\n################ work/txt/dos-015__piece-02.txt\n\n===== PAGE 1 (textlen=705, images=5) =====\nSERVICE REPORT\nMaintenance and metrological check\nREPORT ID\nLS-RI-2024-6488\nPO NUMBER\nPO-842735\nPAGE\n1/5\nDATE OF INTERVENTION\n2024-06-08\nJOB NO.\nAFF-24600\nISSUE DATE\n2024-06-12\nREQUEST DATE\n2024-05-30\nINSTALLATION\nLine 3\nrotary filling machine\nCUSTOMER\nBelquin Foods\nHead office: Wrexham\nSITE\nWexford Works\nS/N\nTO312707\nMACHINE\nHelorquin 160\nMANUFACTURER\nASSET NO.\nINV-87229\nSCOPE\nMetrological check and preventive\nmaintenance of dosing equipment\nSTATUS\nCompliant\nNon-compliant\nTo be reviewed\nSign-off\nPrepared by\nChecked by\nApproved by\nName\nOwen Doyle\nChloe Thornley\nOlivia Gallagher\nDate\n2024-06-12\n2024-06-14\nSignature\nRev.\nDate\nDescription\nA\n2024-06-12\nFirst issue\nB\n2024-06-14\nCorrected after review\n\n===== PAGE 2 (textlen=1012, images=1) =====\nLororzor Services Ltd\nDocument ref. LS-RI-2024-6488  Revision B\nPrinted on 2024-06-30\nPage 2/5\n1. Visit\nFIELD TEAM\nOwen Doyle (lead)\nCallum Calloway (assistant)\nREQUESTED BY\nRyan Keane\nTIMES\nArrival: 8 h 00\nDuration: 2.5 h\nDrive motor rating plate.\nInstrument\nMake\nSerial\nCalibrated\nreference flow meter\nPolamos\nIN-71767\n2023-09-15\nprecision balance\nPraiorix\nIN-5338